messages:
olivia: Heads up 1514 found a docs/runtime mismatch for chat streaming events. The API ref shows SSE events emitted as `event: token` with payload `{\"token\": \"...\"}`, but the server emits `event: message` with `{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"...\"}`. This broke one of our quickstarts.

kevin: ouch. Which page(s) are wrong?

olivia: `docs/reference/chat#streaming` and the JS SDK streaming example in the quickstart. The OpenAPI example was updated last quarter to use the `token` envelope shape, but runtime team stabilized on `message` (more generic).

maria: do we prefer changing docs to match runtime or vice versa?

kevin: runtime choice is intentionalwe standardized on `message` to support non-token events (tool calls, structured blocks). Docs should reflect that.

amy: I'll open a PR to update the reference and the quickstart snippets to the `message` envelope. Also will add a short compatibility note: older clients might expect `token`; include a tiny example to convert `message` -> token stream for naive parsers.

santiago: good call. Can you add a sample SSE parser for curl and node? Many folks copy/paste curl `--no-buffer` examples.

amy: yes. Proposed examples:

```
# curl SSE parse (bash)
curl -N -H "Accept: text/event-stream" \
  -d '{"input":"hello"}' https://api.redwood.ai/chat/stream | \
  while read -r line; do
    # server sends: event: message\ndata: {"role":"assistant","content":"hi"}\n
    if [[ $line == data:* ]]; then
      payload=${line#data: }
      echo "RECV ROLE: $(jq -r .role <<< $payload)";
      echo "RECV CONTENT: $(jq -r .content <<< $payload)";
    fi
  done
```

```js
// node SSE: convert message events to token chunks for old clients
const es = new EventSource(url);
es.addEventListener('message', e => {
  const obj = JSON.parse(e.data);
  if (obj.content) {
    // emit token-chunks (simple split)
    obj.content.split(/\s+/).forEach(tok => {
      // old libs expect: {token: "..."}
      console.log(JSON.stringify({token: tok}));
    });
  }
});
```

kevin: nice. Also update the SDK streaming helper docs to show reading `role`+`content` and handling structured events (e.g., `tool_call`).

maria: I'll add a smoke-test to the docs CI that starts a local streaming mock and asserts the `event: message` envelope in the first event. Saves us from regressions.

docs-bot: Issue #678 linked. PR #2401 created by amy (draft): updates `docs/reference/chat/streaming`, quickstart snippets, node/curl examples, and adds migration note. Checklist: run smoke tests, update openapi example, update SDK snippets.

olivia: one more: update the changelog entry for the streaming shape change and add a short line in the migration guide describing how to map `message` -> `token` for older clients.

kevin: I'll coordinate a tiny runtime note in the release notes so customers running proxies know about the envelope change.

amy: merging PR after a quick review. tagging @maria for CI verification.

docs-bot: PR #2401 merged to main. Docs site redeploy scheduled. Migration note added under `/docs/migrations/streaming-event-envelope.md`.

maria: smoke tests pass on staging. Examples updated and verified with Node and curl. Closing thread. :white_check_mark:
